id: pm-brief-gtiy
title: Enforce genuine 100/100/100/100 source coverage in the release gate
description: "The built-in Node coverage baseline for dist/index.js is 82.84% lines, 74.67% branches, and 92.19% functions. Add meaningful unit, integration, functional, and real-CLI tests for every reachable source path; exclude only generated or non-source artifacts with documented justification. Enforce 100% lines, branches, functions, and statements in release:check without ignore pragmas, artificial calls, or coverage manipulation."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T13:52:29.218Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T16:26:04.009Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#e067658fb6e4485ee2d1dfa3"
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "A deterministic coverage command reports 100% lines, branches, functions, and statements for all source files; release:check fails when any source coverage dimension drops below 100%; Tests exercise observable behavior and real failure paths without coverage-only branches, mocks that bypass production behavior, ignore pragmas, or generated-code inflation; Coverage execution uses the project-local latest pm CLI and is stable in npm and bun workflows"
risk: high
severity: high
component: testing
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author}:
  pm-brief-q325,related,"2026-07-26T13:52:29.218Z",codex
notes[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T13:52:41.808Z",codex,"Baseline measured 2026-07-26 with Node built-in coverage against the latest project-local pm CLI: dist/index.js 82.84% lines, 74.67% branches, 92.19% functions. The aggregate report is lower because it also observes a temporary installed extension copy; the source file row is the actionable baseline."
  "2026-07-26T14:13:07.264Z",codex,"Workflow-level acceptance evidence is now linked in addition to the reporting-only coverage baseline. This Issue remains open until release:check itself enforces all four 100% thresholds; a passing current release:check is not evidence that the acceptance criteria are met."
  "2026-08-02T00:42:20.038Z","harness:codex","TDD tranche 1: added a real registered-command acceptance matrix covering all nine command families, host-global JSON, Slack/JSON/Markdown output, output-file persistence, real PM reads, duplicate/governance SDK scans, activity deltas, and Git divergence. Targeted test passes. Full suite now passes 161 tests and source coverage improved from 91.97/76.72/95.85 to 94.86% lines, 78.71% branches, and 96.27% functions. The issue remains in progress; thresholds are intentionally unchanged until meaningful tests reach exact 100/100/100."
  "2026-08-07T07:30:38.541Z","harness:codex","TDD tranche 2 on release head v2026.08.07: rebased the registered-command acceptance matrix onto current main; removed two zero-use production helpers; added behavior-driven coverage for text ranking with confidence and explanations,typed focus parsing,staleness and momentum text output,invalid positive and non-negative integer flags,default-branch discovery through local main and origin/HEAD,and deterministic ordering across multiple real SDK duplicate clusters. The suite now covers 294/294 functions (100%),4383/4547 lines (96.39%),and 1148/1434 branches (80.06%). @unbrained/pm-cli resolves to latest 2026.8.6 and pm-changelog to latest 2026.8.7. Exact line/branch coverage remains open; thresholds intentionally remain at the existing ratchet until genuine behavior reaches 100/100/100."
  "2026-08-07T07:37:01.435Z","harness:codex","CI round 1 found a runner-topology assumption in the new acceptance matrix: actions/checkout leaves a detached HEAD without a local main ref,so the clean divergence fixture failed before later command cases ran. Production correctly rejected the unknown ref. The fixture now compares HEAD with HEAD,preserving the clean-divergence contract without assuming branch refs. Targeted registered-command test and typecheck pass."
  "2026-08-07T07:39:30.482Z","harness:codex","Review round 1 accepted three CodeRabbit findings: the privacy blocker now links explicit future fail-closed identity and all-ref content audit commands; typed-focus and ID-focus are independent behavioral assertions; and origin/HEAD points to trunk so its resolution cannot pass through the main fallback. The privacy commands are acceptance contracts and are not claimed green while the published-history blocker remains open."
  "2026-08-07T07:46:28.551Z","harness:codex","Companion reconciliation corrected the history-identity finding: pm-cli-website-ikjv explicitly accepts the personal identities forward-only,and pm-cli-website-ktip states the approved allowlist contains exactly three addresses including the observed one. pm-brief-yigc is canceled as a false positive,its unimplemented audit contracts were removed,and it is no longer linked as a release blocker."
  "2026-08-07T08:23:00.029Z","harness:codex","Coverage round 3 (2026-08-07): added behavior-driven acceptance for required-vs-optional pm reader failures, empty/filter-narrowed insights, Slack guidance, Git discovery/read failures, complete storage-integrity findings on a real corrupted tracker, output persistence across command families, bounded high-severity divergence, delta budgets, and lifecycle transitions. TDD exposed and fixed a real bug where close->reopen remained counted/rendered as Closed; lifecycle classification now follows the latest close/cancel/reopen transition and close->reopen->close is covered. Full coverage after the first two slices reached 98.17% lines / 82.05% branches / 100% functions (178 tests); final post-PM release gates still pending and exact 100/100/100 remains open."
  "2026-08-07T08:28:25.010Z","harness:codex","Final round-3 measurement: 187 tests; index.ts 100.00% lines, 84.89% branches, 100.00% functions. Required line/function coverage is now exact, while exact branch coverage remains intentionally open; no threshold was weakened and no exclusion was added. npm run release:check passed before the final fault-injection additions (typecheck/build/coverage, 0 production vulnerabilities, pack dry-run, changelog check); the final full release check will be rerun on this exact tree."
  "2026-08-07T08:42:06.431Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review identified two actionable gaps on PR #58: the PM item did not link Bun CI evidence, and direct pm.cmd execution was unsafe on Windows. Added the Bun release-check command as linked evidence and changed pm execution to invoke the resolved project-local CLI entry through process.execPath without a shell. Extracted output parsers so malformed-envelope coverage remains behavior-focused without replacing the CLI executable."
  "2026-08-07T08:45:01.920Z","harness:codex","Executed the newly linked Bun gate through pm test on the exact review-remediation tree: Bun 1.3.5 installed the npm-lock-backed project and bun run release:check passed all 187 tests, 100.00% lines, 85.99% branches, 100.00% functions, production audit, package dry-run, and changelog validation. Bun emitted its known duplicate dependency warning because pm-cli is intentionally both a runtime dependency and a development dependency for an extension package; no generated bun.lock is retained."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,Source coverage target
  test/brief.test.ts,project,Coverage test expansion
tests[3]{command,path,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  "bun install --no-save && bun run release:check",.github/workflows/ci.yml,project,1800
  "NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npm run release:check",.github/workflows/ci.yml,project,1800
  "npm run build && npm run build:test && node --experimental-test-coverage --test dist-test/*.js",test/brief.test.ts,project,1800
body: "2026-08-07 compatibility-boundary tranche: upgraded both runtime and development @unbrained/pm-cli ranges/lock resolution from 2026.8.6 to latest 2026.8.7; added behavior-driven coverage for current/legacy pm item, next, compact-activity, and full-activity envelopes; malformed-row rejection; sparse/default fields; clamped limits; stable chronological ties; legacy relationship target keys; and evidence-link object shapes. Fresh project-local evidence: npm test 192/192 pass; npm run coverage reports index.ts 100.00% lines, 88.14% branches, 100.00% functions (up from fresh 86.06% branch baseline, no ignore pragmas or coverage exemptions). Exact 100/100/100/100 and executable scripts/coverage-gate.ts inclusion remain open; do not close or publish.\n\nRelease-gate follow-up: NPM_CONFIG_USERCONFIG=/dev/null npm run release:check passed end to end with 192/192 tests, 100.00% lines, 88.07% branches, 100.00% functions, zero production vulnerabilities, successful package dry-run, and current changelog. The standalone coverage run reported 88.14%; record the conservative repeat-run value 88.07% because Node V8 branch accounting varies slightly with exercised integration-process paths. Exact coverage remains open.\n\nBun parity follow-up: bun 1.3.5 install and bun run release:check passed with the same 192/192 tests, 100.00/88.07/100.00 line/branch/function report, zero production vulnerabilities, package dry-run, and changelog check. Removed the redundant devDependency copy of @unbrained/pm-cli so Bun no longer warns about duplicate dependency declarations; the runtime dependency remains ^2026.8.7. Latest pm merge install also added non-merge protection plus managed JSON merging for .agents/pm/extensions paths."
